📚 JavaScript DOM Notes (Chai aur Code)

1️⃣ document.getElementById("title")
➡️ Use: ID ke through element select karta hai.

Example:
document.getElementById("title")

Output:
<h1 id="title" class="heading">DOM learning on Chai aur Code</h1>

----------------------------------------------------

2️⃣ document.getElementById("title").id

➡️ Use: Element ki ID return karta hai.

Example:
document.getElementById("title").id

Output:
"title"

----------------------------------------------------

3️⃣ document.getElementById("title").class

➡️ Use: JavaScript me .class naam ki koi property nahi hoti.

Example:
document.getElementById("title").class

Output:
undefined

✅ Correct Property:
.className

----------------------------------------------------

4️⃣ document.getElementById("title").className

➡️ Use: Element ka class name return karta hai.

Output:
"heading"

----------------------------------------------------

5️⃣ document.getElementById("title").getAttribute

➡️ Use: Function ko show karta hai.

Output:
ƒ getAttribute() { [native code] }

----------------------------------------------------

6️⃣ document.getElementById("title").getAttribute()

➡️ Use: Ye galat hai kyuki attribute ka naam pass nahi kiya.

Output:
TypeError

Correct Syntax:

element.getAttribute("attributeName")

----------------------------------------------------

7️⃣ document.getElementById("title").getAttribute("id")

➡️ Use: ID attribute ki value return karta hai.

Output:
"title"

----------------------------------------------------

8️⃣ document.getElementById("title").getAttribute("class")

➡️ Use: Class attribute ki value return karta hai.

Output:
"heading"

----------------------------------------------------

9️⃣ document.getElementById("title").setAttribute("class","sam")

➡️ Use: Existing class ko replace kar deta hai.

Before:
class="heading"

After:
class="sam"

----------------------------------------------------

🔟 const title = document.getElementById("title")

➡️ Use: Element ko variable me store karta hai taaki baar-baar getElementById() na likhna pade.

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣1️⃣ title.style.backgroundColor = "green"

➡️ Use: Background color change karta hai.

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣2️⃣ title.style.padding = "15px"

➡️ Use: Padding add karta hai.

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣3️⃣ title.style.borderRadius = 25px

❌ Wrong

Reason:
CSS values string me likhi jati hain.

✅ Correct

title.style.borderRadius = "25px"

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣4️⃣ title.innerHTML

➡️ Use: HTML + Text dono return karta hai.

Example Output:

DOM learning on Chai aur Code
<span style="display:none">Test case</span>

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣5️⃣ title.innerText

➡️ Use: Sirf visible text return karta hai.

Output:

DOM learning on Chai aur Code

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣6️⃣ title.textContent

➡️ Use: Visible + Hidden dono text return karta hai.

Output:

DOM learning on Chai aur Code Test case

----------------------------------------------------

Difference

innerHTML ➜ HTML + Text

innerText ➜ Sirf Visible Text

textContent ➜ Visible + Hidden Text

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣7️⃣ document.getElementsByClassName("heading")

➡️ Use: Same class wale sare elements return karta hai.

Output:

HTMLCollection

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣8️⃣ document.querySelector("h1")

➡️ Use: Pehla h1 select karta hai.

----------------------------------------------------

1️⃣9️⃣ document.querySelector("h2")

➡️ Use: Pehla h2 select karta hai.

Output:

<h2>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet.</h2>

----------------------------------------------------

2️⃣0️⃣ const myul = document.querySelector("ul")

➡️ Use: Pehla ul select karta hai.

----------------------------------------------------

2️⃣1️⃣ myul.querySelector("li")

➡️ Use: UL ke andar pehla LI select karta hai.

----------------------------------------------------

2️⃣2️⃣ const turngreen = myul.querySelector("li")

➡️ Use: LI ko variable me store karta hai.

----------------------------------------------------

2️⃣3️⃣ turngreen.style.backgroundColor = "greem"

❌ Wrong

Reason:
"greem" koi valid CSS color nahi hai.

Browser ignore kar dega.

✅ Correct

turngreen.style.backgroundColor = "green"

----------------------------------------------------

2️⃣4️⃣ turngreen.style.padding = "10px"

➡️ Use: LI ke andar padding add karta hai.

----------------------------------------------------

2️⃣5️⃣ turngreen.style.borderRadius = "15px"

➡️ Use: LI ke corners round karta hai.

----------------------------------------------------

⭐ Extra Important Commands

document.querySelector("#id")
➡️ ID select karta hai.

document.querySelector(".class")
➡️ Class select karta hai.

document.querySelectorAll("li")
➡️ Sare matching elements return karta hai.
Output:
NodeList

document.getElementsByTagName("li")
➡️ Sare LI elements return karta hai.
Output:
HTMLCollection

title.classList
➡️ Classes manage karne ke liye.

title.classList.add("active")
➡️ Class add karta hai.

title.classList.remove("active")
➡️ Class remove karta hai.

title.classList.toggle("active")
➡️ Hai to remove, nahi hai to add.

title.classList.contains("active")
➡️ true/false return karta hai.

document.createElement("div")
➡️ Naya HTML element banata hai.

parent.appendChild(child)
➡️ Child add karta hai.

title.remove()
➡️ Element delete karta hai.

title.parentElement
➡️ Parent element return karta hai.

title.children
➡️ Sare child elements return karta hai.

ul.firstElementChild
➡️ Pehla child.

ul.lastElementChild
➡️ Last child.

li.nextElementSibling
➡️ Next sibling.

li.previousElementSibling
➡️ Previous sibling.

title.tagName
➡️ Tag name return karta hai.
Output:
H1

title.nodeName
➡️ Node name return karta hai.
Output:
H1

input.value
➡️ Input ki value.

checkbox.checked
➡️ Checkbox selected hai ya nahi.

img.src
➡️ Image ka URL.

img.alt
➡️ Image ka alternate text.

link.href
➡️ Link ka URL.

====================================================

